{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792497833,"nonce":"T46kgUcbbNfkSuEZq7YcmwdHufs=","message":"The final-source normal and forced VB tests pass so far, including eight new RGBA cases, seven existing composite GPU cases plus its CPU fingerprint case, four motion cases, and the normal native regression set (producer2, overlay7, aux2, display-list33, fill-rule1). Forced DT and the full gate follow. Temporary overrides are confined to the probe driver and restored before the gate.\n\nImagePaintOrder records primitive/path cursors and the command count in the active background owner. Ordered nodes merge image draws around Push/Pop boundaries, including image-only groups whose primitive cursors never advance. Images retain explicit/unrepresented alpha; represented group opacity is composed once. Clear, legacy overlay, ordered overlay1/4, render_msaa resolve, tight bake, reduced backdrop and glass-frame entry points now dispatch ordered background images. Full-batch consumers use render_unordered_dynamic_images for remaining foreground records; the explicit render_dynamic_images API still draws its supplied sequence unconditionally.\n\nCanvas collection retains whole per-callback background batches when ordered images are present and keeps their original aux arrays. Foreground primitives retain rebased merged aux data. Callbacks get a visit sequence independent of primitive count, and matching dynamic callbacks are recorded even when image-only or currently empty. This resolves sort ties between an image-only callback and a later callback starting at the same primitive cursor. The actual direct/compositor two-frame test covers changing pixel bytes, two same-z callbacks with equal primitive starts, image-only groups, foreground meshes, and single blending of translucent positive-z content. Compositor fixture texture usage was corrected to include COPY_DST; that validation error was a fixture mistake, not a renderer fix.\n\nImage bytes/geometry/clips/cursors are included in scratch fingerprints. Primitive-only canvas splicing, motion patching, CSS patching and damaged-static repaint bail for ordered images. App dispatch keeps image-only dynamic batches, avoids duplicate path passes, and excludes already-rendered ordered content from later primitive-only z overlays. Invalid/empty/overflow-sized RGBA uploads are rejected before allocation or GPU texture creation.\n\nLimits remain in the parents: foreground-only RGBA records are explicitly separate and keep current effective opacity; general foreground group isolation, groups spanning independent streams, separately collected text/SVG/images and named Sample are unchanged. Native draw_rgba_pixels retains its AABB transform and rectangular/rounded clip contract; circle/ellipse/polygon/path clip completeness and arbitrary affine image transforms are not implemented by this slice. Do not close 369499d or e0a7502 on this child. No timing, memory, browser or mobile measurements are claimed.","files":null}]}